## Key Patterns

### Auto-Provisioning
1. Scanner boots → connects to "setup" WiFi
2. Broadcasts UDP: `{"mac": "aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff"}` on port 9000
3. Tablet listens → shows in UI
4. User taps "Provision" → POSTs config to scanner:8888
5. Scanner saves, reboots → connects to site WiFi

### Zone-Based Tracking
```kotlin
// For each beacon:
val zoneRssiMap = scanners.associate { scanner ->
    scanner.zoneId to scanner.getRssi(beaconMac)
}
val bestZone = zoneRssiMap.maxByOrNull { it.value }?.key

// Only emit event if:
if (newZone != previousZone && dwellTime > 10.seconds) {
    httpClient.post("/api/asset/movement") {
        body = MovementEvent(from = previousZone, to = newZone)
    }
}
```

### Long-Polling Pattern (Runtime API)
```python
# Master Pi watches for zone map changes
current_version = 0
while True:
    response = requests.get(
        "http://api:8000/api/runtime/scanner-zone-map/watch",
        params={"version": current_version},
        timeout=65
    )
    data = response.json()
    scanner_zone_map = data["scanner_zone_map"]
    current_version = data["version"]
    update_local_mappings(scanner_zone_map)
```

### Foreground Service Pattern
```kotlin
class BleScannerService : Service() {
    override fun onStartCommand(): Int {
        startForeground(NOTIFICATION_ID, notification)
        startComponents() // broker, scanner, bridge
        startWatchdog()   // health checks every 60s
        return START_STICKY // auto-restart on crash
    }
}
```

### MQTT QoS 1 (At-Least-Once)
- Acknowledged delivery (broker sends PUBACK)
- Retry on failure (exponential backoff)
- Acceptable duplicates (<0.5%, filtered at app layer)
- Balance: Reliable without QoS 2 overhead

### Single Async Client (No Recreate)
```kotlin
fun connect() {
    if (!isConnecting.compareAndSet(false, true)) return
    if (mqttClient == null) {
        mqttClient = MqttAsyncClient(...) // ONLY IF NULL
        mqttClient?.setCallback(autoReconnectCallback)
    }
    mqttClient?.connect(optionsWithAutoReconnect)
}
// Prevents reconnection storms
```

